# Criterion 1 - hooks inside a git worktree

Run by the orchestrating session on 2026-09-26, macOS 24.6.0, Flutter stable
3.47.0, from a real `git worktree add`-created worktree outside `.claude/`.

Criterion 1 asks for two transcripts: the failing case BEFORE the fix, and the
passing case AFTER. Only the second could be produced. The first is recorded
here as NOT REPRODUCIBLE on this machine, with the measurements that explain
why, rather than being manufactured.

## Setup

    $ ./scripts/dev/setup_git_hooks.sh      # copies into .git/hooks/, does not set core.hooksPath
    $ git worktree add -b probe/140-hook-check <scratch>/wt140 origin/main
    $ cd <scratch>/wt140 && flutter pub get

## 1. The hook really does receive GIT_DIR

A throwaway hook dumping its environment, invoked by a plain `git commit`
from inside the worktree:

    PROBE GIT_DIR=[/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git/worktrees/wt140]
    PROBE GIT_WORK_TREE=[<unset>]
    PROBE GIT_INDEX_FILE=[/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git/worktrees/wt140/index]

So the precondition the fix defends against is present.

## 2. That GIT_DIR really does make Flutter misread itself

    $ flutter --version | head -1
    Flutter 3.47.0 • channel stable • https://github.com/flutter/flutter.git

    $ GIT_DIR=$(git rev-parse --git-dir) flutter --version | head -1
    Flutter 3.49.0-0.1.pre • channel [user-branch] • https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter.git

Flutter shells out to git to identify itself, and an inherited GIT_DIR makes
that lookup read THIS repository. It reports the project's own remote and
branch as the SDK's. The mechanism in the issue is real and is measured here.

## 3. AFTER the fix: a commit inside the worktree succeeds - PASS

    $ git commit -m "chore: probe that hooks run inside a git worktree"
    Running pre-commit checks...
    📝 Checking code formatting...
    Formatted 367 files (0 changed) in 1.27 seconds.
    🔍 Running flutter analyze...
    Analyzing wt140...
    No issues found! (ran in 2.8s)
    ✅ Pre-commit checks passed.
    [probe/140-hook-check a489fa5] chore: probe that hooks run inside a git worktree

`commit-msg` also ran and was exercised: an earlier attempt using the subject
`probe:` was rejected for not being a Conventional Commit type, which is
criterion 4's hook behaving correctly inside a worktree.

## 4. BEFORE the fix: NOT REPRODUCIBLE - documented deviation

The pre-fix hook was restored verbatim from `c7f5713` (the commit before the
#140 fix; `grep -c GIT_DIR` on it returns 0) and the same commit re-attempted
in the same worktree:

    Got dependencies!
    Analyzing wt140...
    No issues found! (ran in 7.1s)
    ✅ Pre-commit checks passed.
    [probe/140-hook-check 7a601a5] chore: probe before-fix hook in a worktree

It passed. No failing transcript exists to commit, and none was fabricated.

### Why it does not fail here, precisely

The misread version is `3.49.0-0.1.pre`, which still satisfies
`environment: sdk: ^3.8.0` in `pubspec.yaml`. Nothing rejects it.

The `0.0.0-unknown` symptom the issue reports needs `git describe` to fail
outright, which happens when GIT_DIR points at the repository's main `.git`
(no tag describes its HEAD) rather than at a worktree's git dir. A plain
`git commit` from inside a worktree exports the latter.

So the reported failure depends on which GIT_DIR value is inherited and on tag
reachability - not on being in a worktree as such.

### Why the fix is still correct

It removes a dependency on luck. Today the misread yields a version that
happens to satisfy the constraint; a different SDK checkout, tag state or
constraint turns the same misread into a blocked commit. The hooks now run
Flutter with GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_COMMON_DIR,
GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY, GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES and GIT_PREFIX unset,
so the lookup cannot read this repository at all.

## Cleanup

Worktree removed, `probe/140-hook-check` deleted, the fixed hook restored and
re-verified (3 GIT_DIR references present). Main checkout clean.
